    <comment>- Update to version 0.3.0.0:
  + Support APV RAW encoding and decoding
  + Companding (compressing + expanding) algorithm for coding 16bit
    4 channel linear pixel value
  + New profiles are introduced to distinguish between the
    conventional APV and APV RAW (forwarded request 1362435 from rrahl0)</comment>
    <requestid>1362436</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="11" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>d8039d10c96402be5515acc7a84eeea9</srcmd5>
    <version>1.1.2.0</version>
    <time>1790865832</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 1.1.2.0:
  + Performance:
    - VLC coefficient decoding was reworked:
    - The exp-Golomb prefix is read with a count-leading-zeros
      instead of bit by bit.
    - The bit buffer is topped up with whole bytes before each
      symbol, so the prefix and suffix of a normal code are read in
      one step. The buffer end is never read past.
    - The separate k = 0 readers were removed; all run and level
      codes go through one reader.
    - Decoding is about 20–30% faster at high bitrates and about 8%
      faster at low bitrates, measured on x86 with both single- and
      multi-threaded decoding. The decoded output is bit-exact with
      v1.1.1.0.
  + Correctness and robustness:
    - Dequantization no longer left-shifts negative values or
      overflows int at high QP; the SIMD paths now saturate
      correctly
    - The exp-Golomb prefix sum no longer wraps u32 on malformed
      input, so builds with -fsanitize=unsigned-integer-overflow
      (such as Android) no longer abort
    - The exp-Golomb prefix length is bounded to keep decoded
      values within int
    - Metadata payload_type and payload_size are checked against
      u32 wraparound
    - OAPV_MAX_NUM_META_PAYLOADS is enforced per access unit in
      oapvm_set()
    - Encoder error paths release the input and reconstruction
      image references
    - Reconstructed AC coefficients are checked against the 16-bit (forwarded request 1381542 from iznogood)</comment>
    <requestid>1381652</requestid>
  </revision>
